A. THE GRAIN Q: the pace Q |D| / T_D per direction against 1 / sqrt 3, T_D = isqrt(3 |D|^2 Q^2), over the 290 primitive directions within Manhattan 6
   Q | the largest relative departure | the smallest | the bound 1 / (sqrt 3 Q - 1)
       64 | 7.739e-03 | -2.220e-16 | 9.103e-03
      256 | 9.142e-04 | -2.220e-16 | 2.260e-03
     1024 | 3.497e-04 | -2.220e-16 | 5.641e-04
     4096 | 6.768e-05 | -2.220e-16 | 1.410e-04
    65536 | 6.006e-06 | -2.220e-16 | 8.810e-06
   the anisotropy of c falls as 1 / Q, never below 1 / sqrt 3 (isqrt rounds down): the limit Q -> infinity is isotropic at the rate of the grain

B. THE GRAIN N: Born's rung error and the CHSH deficit
   N | the rung's error bound 1 / (2 N) | the CHSH bound 8 / N | the registered S | 2 sqrt 2 - S
      64 | 7.81e-03 | 1.25e-01 | 2.750000 | 7.84e-02
     256 | 1.95e-03 | 3.12e-02 | 2.812500 | 1.59e-02
    1024 | 4.88e-04 | 7.81e-03 | 2.828125 | 3.02e-04
    4096 | 1.22e-04 | 1.95e-03 | 2.828125 | 3.02e-04
   65536 | 7.63e-06 | 1.22e-04 | 11585 / 4096 = 2.828369 (the closed form) | 5.8e-05
   Born and Tsirelson are limits in N at the rate 1 / N; the tables' 1 / 256 stays as a floor (2.1e-6 in S with the tables fixed)

C. THE GRAIN P: the fraction of a shell's Nodes on some line of the fan within Manhattan P (the field against the comb)
   r | P = 4 | P = 6 | P = 8 | P = 12
    4 |  65.7 % | 100.0 % | 100.0 % | 100.0 %
    6 |  31.6 % |  62.7 % | 100.0 % | 100.0 %
    8 |  17.1 % |  42.3 % |  78.0 % | 100.0 %
   10 |  10.4 % |  31.5 % |  56.5 % |  98.1 %
   12 |   5.8 % |  20.0 % |  45.1 % |  86.8 %
   16 |   5.0 % |  14.1 % |  29.2 % |  65.8 %
   20 |   2.8 % |   8.9 % |  18.2 % |  50.1 %
   the fans: P = 4: 98 directions, P = 6: 290 directions, P = 8: 674 directions, P = 12: 2114 directions
   a shell is covered while r is below about P / 2 and becomes a comb beyond it: the crowd is a field only where P >> r (DERIVATIONS 3.2's limit); the registered fans (P = 6 in space, 7 on the plane) are combs beyond r = 4

D. THE SHELL MEANS' RIPPLE AGAINST THE CONTINUUM'S 1 / r^2 AND 1 / r, per P (q = the fan's size)
   P | q | P r^2 over r = 4 .. 14: the mean, the least, the largest, over q sqrt 3 / (4 pi) | A r likewise over 3 q / (4 pi)
    4 |    98 | 0.977, 0.805, 1.144 | 0.974, 0.812, 1.128
    6 |   290 | 0.991, 0.880, 1.118 | 0.993, 0.883, 1.118
    8 |   674 | 0.977, 0.873, 1.118 | 0.982, 0.889, 1.116
   12 |  2114 | 0.986, 0.915, 1.077 | 0.992, 0.933, 1.076
   the shell means carry the 1 / r^2 and 1 / r forms at every P within the ripple; the ripple is the comb's, and a single Node reads a line or nothing where the shell is not covered
